    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Root Access to the Lattice.</strong> You don’t just <em>look</em> at the underlying structure of the world anymore. You log in.</p><ul><li>Once per <strong>turn</strong>, when your Domain undertakes an operation or encounters an event that clearly hinges on <strong>Sparks, Tikkun, hex-tilt, or metaphysical backlash</strong>, you may invoke this feature.</li><li>The GM rewrites one key metaphysical line-item in the resolution: a catastrophic tilt becomes a severe one, a severe one becomes mild, a Spark backlash becomes a warning, or a dangerous corruption roll is upgraded to a partial or clean result.</li><li>In mechanical terms, this acts like a once-per-turn <strong>metaphysical failsafe / uplift</strong> for Tikkun- and anomaly-heavy operations, similar in scale to your other classes’ capstones. It cannot guarantee success, but it can <em>guarantee that the worst outcome is taken off the table</em>.</li><li>On the story level, this is your graduation: reality now treats you as someone who can file tickets against fundamental behavior and expect them to be respected—eventually.</li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
